  "body": "In #56 it came up that we don't have conventions for \"in parallel\" described. \r\n\r\nI actually think we should have \"threads\" instead of \"in parallel\" that can run tasks or a sequence of tasks and message back, rather than just an unlimited number of threads spawned with \"in parallel\" that lead to all kinds of race conditions when not used properly. See also https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/1843.\r\n\r\nIt might make sense to describe this concept here, but maybe since it often relates to execution IDL or HTML is a better place.",
